Functional Scope of RBGA

RBGA’s functional scope is broad and system-wide. It is not limited to a single app or department; rather, it operates across the entire environment (the “IP stack” of Southern’s intellectual property framework) to
ensure all digital actions remain within governed parameters
minttologic.medium.com
. Key aspects of RBGA’s scope include:

Real-time Oversight of Behavior: RBGA acts as a runtime authority layer “watching” behavior across the environment and evaluating it against policies and norms in real time
minttologic.medium.com
. Unlike simple static guardrails, it considers context and evolving conditions. For example, it can monitor multiple AI agents or services simultaneously, observing how they interact and make decisions.

Decision-Making Accountability: The authority focuses on keeping decision-making aligned with human-approved rules and ethics. It creates a safety net around autonomous operations
minttologic.medium.com
. If an AI or software agent begins to stray (e.g. an LLM agent veers into disallowed actions or a transaction looks fraudulent), RBGA detects this through behavioral signals. This ensures AI “capability never 
outruns custody” – the system’s power is kept in check by oversight
minttologic.medium.com
.

Environment-Level (External) Governance: RBGA operates at the environment level rather than inside an agent’s mind. This means it provides governance around the agents (much like air-traffic control oversees airplanes) 
instead of relying on the agents to police themselves
minttologic.medium.com
minttologic.medium.com
. (As Southern clarifies, an AI’s self-reflection is just internal “self-talk,” whereas RBGA is an external authority with receipts and remedies for misconduct
minttologic.medium.com
.) It watches across tools, users, and even across organizations if necessary, making it a cross-cutting oversight layer.

Licensing and Credentials: Part of RBGA’s scope is to license and credential actions. Every action by a user or system must hold a valid “minted” credential to execute. RBGA can issue or verify these licenses across 
different tiers (user level, system level, protocol level)
